course: dictionary
lesson: 7411
title: Poisonous: staying safe, and words that hurt
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Poisonous means containing poison. Something poisonous can make you very ill, or even kill you, if you eat it, drink it, breathe it in or touch it. «Many berries that look tasty are poisonous» is a warning: looking nice does not make something safe.
explain: The word can also describe people. When it is used this way, it means very unkind and harmful, like a poison that hurts feelings instead of the body. This is figurative, so the word is used like a picture, not about real poison.
explain: Context helps you check. «Gran's "never mix bleach with other cleaners" is completely true: some mixtures give off poisonous gas.» Gas is dangerous even when you cannot see it, so the clue is the danger, not how something looks.
fact: Poisonous means containing poison, and able to make you very ill or kill you.
fact: «Poisonous» can also describe very unkind and harmful remarks, used figuratively.
fact: Never eat anything from the wild unless an adult who knows says it is safe.
fact: Bleach, cleaners and some medicines can be poisonous, so keep them out of reach and never take too much medicine.
fact: Animals that bite or sting with poison are venomous; poison dart frogs are poisonous to eat or touch.
exercise: «Lilies are very poisonous to cats.» What does poisonous mean here? | *Able to make a cat very ill | Brightly coloured | Soft and fluffy | Very tasty to eat
exercise: «Collect conkers, acorns and pine cones for crafts, but never eat conkers or acorns, because they are poisonous.» Which of these must you never eat? | Toast | *Acorns | Pasta | Carrots
exercise: «The poisonous remarks made Sam cry.» What does poisonous mean in this sentence? | Full of light | Covered in poison | *Very unkind and harmful | Very kind and helpful
test: What is the safe thing to do with wild berries? | Taste one to check | Eat them if they look tasty | *Leave them alone unless an adult who knows says they are safe | Share them with friends
test: Which of these is a household product that can be poisonous? | Sugar | *Bleach | Bread | Milk
exam: What does «highly poisonous» mean? | *Very able to make you very ill or kill you | Easy to clean | Very tasty | Slightly sticky
